{
  "reason": "The current LightGCN achieves macro validation HR@10 of 0.57, but Electronics reaches only 0.35 versus the SASRec baseline's 0.42; fixed propagation-depth averaging is a plausible limitation, not an established cause. Modify model_design to learn the depth mixture and training_evaluation to verify optimization and exported-predictor consistency. Historical successes support preserving target-excluded profiles, while failed sampling and loss experiments favor isolating this architecture change without reverting the current parent's settings.",
  "module": [
    "model_design",
    "training_evaluation"
  ],
  "plan": {
    "data_processing_and_feature_engineering": null,
    "model_design": "Add self.layer_logits = nn.Parameter(torch.zeros(3)) to each independently instantiated LightGCN, preserving its constructor and all existing method signatures. In encode(), compute weights = torch.softmax(self.layer_logits, dim=0), then replace total / 3.0 with the differentiable weighted sum of the initial embedding and the existing two successive sparse propagation outputs, preserving x, total, and the returned user/item tensor shapes. Zero initialization reproduces uniform weighting, while learned category-specific weights test whether different propagation depths improve representations without additional graph passes. Ensure training_vectors(), target_excluded_vectors(), and export() all consume this same encode() result, retaining differentiable repeated-target exclusion and materializing the learned mixture into the existing PredictionModel buffers. Keep graph construction, DIM=64, item biases, history coefficient 0.5, ten-interaction half-life, and PredictionModel.forward() unchanged.",
    "training_evaluation": "Preserve train_dataset(ds, device, deadline), its variables, and Adam(model.parameters(), lr=0.003), which automatically includes layer_logits; retain the existing raw-embedding/bias regularizer without adding a mixture penalty. Add small deterministic fixtures under forked RNG state that verify zero-logit equivalence to the original average, nonuniform-mixture agreement with an explicit three-layer sum, and finite nonzero ranking-loss gradients to layer_logits on an asymmetric graph. Extend write_predict_script() checks to export a model with nonuniform logits, save and reload its materialized checkpoint, and compare direct validation scores with scores from the generated predictor's actual loader; keep its signature, dataset routing, and checkpoint buffer format unchanged because inference consumes the already mixed embeddings. Explicitly preserve preprocessing seed 0, training seed 42, supplied splits, all four categories, DATA_DIR = os.environ['GAGC_DATA_DIR'], recency-weighted positive sampling, 32 uniform unseen negatives with replacement, sampled-softmax loss, optimization settings, batch size, steps, SASREC_EPOCHS default 200, stopping limits, and HR@10 checkpoint selection with NDCG@10 tie-breaking. Assess macro HR@10 against 0.57 and Electronics against 0.35 using the unchanged pinned 200-user/category, 99-unique-negative, seed-42 validation protocol, retaining single-GPU execution, trial-local artifacts, the shared 43,200 GPU-second budget, and no hidden-test access or host-evaluator changes."
  }
}
